    "# 2. Setup\n",
    "## 2.1 Data Loading\n",
    "I start by loading the signal sample and the three background samples: Diboson, Z+jets, and Top. Before doing the analysis, I check the main variables I use in the study for missing values, and in this case no extra cleaning is needed.\n",
    "\n",
    "For plotting and fitting, I convert the mass-type variables from MeV to GeV because the numbers are much easier to read that way in the figures. I do not change the event weights, since those must stay the same throughout the analysis. When needed, I also merge the three background samples into a single combined background sample.\n",
    "\n",
    "One important point here is that the event yield is not simply the number of rows in the dataframe. In this project, the meaningful yield comes from the sum of `FullEventWeight`, because these weights are what set the correct relative contribution of each process."
   ]
  },
