    "## 2.2 Kinematic distributions and choice of cuts\n",
    "I first look at the kinematic distributions of the main input variables to see where the signal and background are separated most clearly. Since the project specifically asks for simple square cuts chosen by eye, I use these overlaid plots to guide the selection instead of doing a full optimisation.\n",
    "\n",
    "I tested several cut values before choosing the final ones. The aim was not simply to make the biggest possible signal bump appear, but to find a sensible balance. The cuts should reduce the background and make any signal more visible, while still keeping a mass spectrum that looks smooth enough to fit properly afterwards.\n",
    "\n",
    "Because of that, I do not apply any direct cut on `reco_zv_mass`, and I also avoid making the cuts too aggressive. This is important because very hard cuts can sculpt the mass distribution, which would make the background shape less trustworthy in the later fit. That is also in line with the warning given in the project brief."
   ]
  },
