    "\n",
    "To measure how much the cuts help, I compare the weighted signal and background yields before and after the selection. Before applying any cuts, the weighted signal yield is 4200.16, while the total weighted background is about 5.40 million. After the cuts, the signal yield drops to 2901.36 and the background falls much more strongly to 511349.75.\n",
    "\n",
    "This means the signal efficiency is 0.6908, so around 69% of the signal is kept, while the background efficiency is 0.0946, so only about 9.5% of the background remains. This is a good sign because it shows the cuts are much harder on the background than on the signal.\n",
    "\n",
    "The usual sensitivity numbers also improve clearly. The value of `S/B` increases from 0.000777 to 0.005674, and `S/sqrt(B)` increases from 1.81 to 4.06. So even though some signal is lost, the overall separation becomes much better after the selection.\n",
    "\n",
    "This is the main numerical check for the cut-based part of the analysis. The project asks for a weighted before-and-after comparison, and these results show that the chosen cuts are reasonable: they keep a useful amount of signal while removing most of the background."
